          "snippet": "In particular, according to equilibrium statistical physics, the fluctuation of a variable around its equilibrium value is proportional to the change of the variable in response to an external perturbation, which is known as the fluctuation-response (or fluctuation-dissipation) relation aka the Einstein relation (18). A generalized fluctuation-response relation also holds true even for nonequilibrium systems linearized near a fixed point (19). However, for SGD-based learning dynamics, the fluctuation-response relation would imply that the variance of a variable (PCA weight) should be larger for a flatter landscape, which is the opposite to the observed inverse relation shown in Fig.",
